# Binary state/artifact markers — deliberately NOT Git LFS.
#
# Decision (2026-11): `models/` bundles, `data/stomar.db` and `*.parquet`
# are intentionally git-tracked state synced between machines (see AGENTS.md
# repo-facts and ROADMAP.md). Git LFS was evaluated and deferred — these
# blobs were committed as regular objects and no `filter.lfs` registration
# exists, so declaring `filter=lfs` here was a lie that would fail any
# future `git add`/checkout of these paths with an unregistered-filter error.
# `-text` keeps git from ever line-ending-renormalizing these binaries.
#
# If LFS is ever adopted, register it (`git lfs install --local`) FIRST,
# then re-add the `filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text` lines in one commit —
# see the ROADMAP artifact-migration item.
*.pt -text
*.pkl -text
*.parquet -text
*.db -text
